## Behaviour and content

State where feedback goes, what information is needed and whether a reply is expected. Use an ordinary link for an external issue tracker and a form only when a real receiving service exists. Preserve typed feedback if submission fails. Explain how to remove private information before posting publicly.

Do not automatically attach household configuration, sensor values or screenshots. Keep a separate support route when users need help completing a task. Feedback must never delay a safety-related action.

## Accessibility and implementation

Keep labels visible, associate errors with fields and announce the submission outcome without moving focus unnecessarily. Test with an empty comment, a long comment, server failure and repeated submission. This example uses local feedback only. The documentation footer links to the real repository issue form; the theme does not create a new HA feedback service.

